{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543705-is-w5-getting-a-new-printing","id":1543705,"title":"Is W5 Getting a New Printing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-13T14:51:11-07:00","id":1543705,"title":"Is W5 Getting a New Printing?","content":"I don't know if this is indicative of anything, but Ingram book distributors is currently stating that physical copies of W5 are no longer in stock from the publisher, indefinitely I didn't even realize Ingram was carrying Renegade products again since they sort of stopped in 2022. Usually, if a book is in still in print, but from another source, Ingram would say so. This wasn't the case. Ingram is still offering a small selection of WOD5 books, as well as assorted other Renegade products. I don't know if this means that Ingram will not be carrying W5 for the foreseeable future or if this means that a new printing is coming out soon. The original printing of W5 did have a rather large number of mistakes. Maybe this is the first hint that Renegade will be correcting them. Either way, this seems to be suspicious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T15:06:02-07:00","id":1543706,"title":"","content":"Maybe...?<br /> <br /> But I would also add that for the last two years Renegade had issues with distribution. For example, Alma Maters had originally been announced to be a Q3 2023 release and it instead came out two months ago because of those distribution-issues. So this could just be a result of those distribution-issues.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, when Renegade re-released the Onyx Path supplements they made some changes to them - and didn't tell anyone about them. So it's possible that this could be a 2nd printing/&quot;edition&quot; of W5 that's different from the first one in some way. Renegade isn't transparent when they do this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}